From: 1Pro-L4R8 <hoangquocvietbk2.13@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:21:53 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Check privileges on the base table of a metadata table

ColumnPrivilege.check skipped every MetadataTable, so a user refused SELECT
on an Iceberg table could read t$files, t$entries, t$manifests, t$partitions
and the other metadata tables, which expose per-column lower and upper
bounds, partition values and row counts of the base table. A user subject to
a row access or column masking policy could read the bounds of masked
columns and of filtered rows the same way.

Reading a metadata table now requires table-level SELECT on its base table
and is refused when a row access or column masking policy on the base table
applies to the user. Metadata collect jobs, which run as root on behalf of an
already-checked query, are not checked.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
